adv_02_attributes_status_plans {
    Outcome: add `@status`, `@tags`, and `@plan` without turning every idea into a form; use write-plan AI lightly; keep attributes slim per project norms.
    Runtime: 8–10 min.
    Related: [attribute] [attribute_configuration] [ai_write_plan]
    @example {
        ```rq
        login_api {
            POST /login validates credentials and starts a session.
            Implementation: ["./src/login.ts"]
            @status in-progress
            @tags (
                auth
                security
            )
            @plan {
                goal: ship email/password login for the demo app
                constraints: must honour [password_rules]; no OAuth in this slice
                steps: validate input; issue session; add audit on failure
                open: rate-limit threshold still undecided
            }
        }
        ```
    }
    @script {
        SCR: Open `login_api`. Add `@status` and `@tags` first — pause.

        VO: Attributes are metadata you opt into. reqlan stays unopinionated about which keys you invent —
            slim attributes beat ceremonial fields you never read.

        SCR: Add `@plan` either by hand or via write-plan / `rq-write-plan`. Edit one line after generation so ownership is visible.

        VO: Plans belong on the idea, in git, next to the prose — not only in a chat transcript.
            Let the model draft; you keep the plan honest.

        SCR: Quick filter in Ideas Summary or status surfaces by `@status` / tags if available.

        VO: Status and tags earn their keep when they drive a view or a search.
            If an attribute never appears in how you navigate, delete it.

        VO: Try this: add `@status draft` to one idea you are not ready to implement, and leave its plan empty on purpose.
    }
    @slides (
        {
            id title
            transition fade
            background brand-dark
            kicker Advanced · 02
            heading Attributes without bloat
            body Opt into metadata. Slim keys beat ceremonial forms.
            asset logo
            notes Attributes are metadata you opt into.
        }
        {
            id status-tags
            transition none
            background brand-panel
            heading Status and tags first
            body Earn their keep when they drive a view or a search.
            code_lang rq
            code status: in-progress / tags: auth, security
            notes Slim attributes beat ceremonial fields you never read.
        }
        {
            id plan
            transition fade
            background brand-panel
            heading Plans live on the idea
            body In git, next to the prose — not only in a chat transcript.
            code_lang rq
            code plan goal: ship email/password login; honour [password_rules]
            notes Let the model draft; you keep the plan honest.
        }
        {
            id try-this
            transition fade
            background brand-dark
            heading Try this
            body Mark one idea @status draft and leave its plan empty on purpose.
            fragments Next — Ideas Summary graph
            notes If an attribute never appears in how you navigate, delete it.
        }
    )
}

