adv_04_context_and_tokens {
    Outcome: steer context dimensions consciously; explain why small slices beat full-graph prompts; practice add-to-context + markdown copy as a habit.
    Runtime: 10 min.
    Related: [context_scope] [llm_first] [ai_integration] [ai_add_to_context]
    @example {
        ```
        // Show a bad prompt vs a good prompt on a slide, then perform the good path live.
        // Bad: "Here's every .rq file in the repo:" + huge paste
        // Good: copied neighbourhood for login_api + one question
        ```
    }
    @script {
        SCR: Open activity bar Scope / context tray. With caret on `login_api`, expand one dimension at a time.

        VO: Context is a composed model — current idea, references, files, optional manual pins —
            not a single blob labelled "the project".

        SCR: Contrast slide: bloated paste vs compact markdown slice. Then copy neighbourhood for `login_api` into chat with one precise question:
            "What tests are missing for empty password rejection?"

        VO: Token discipline is a product feature and a habit.
            Summaries and counts first; expand a dimension when you mean to.

        SCR: Pin one extra idea manually; show it in the tray; unpin.

        VO: Manual context is for the exception you're reasoning about now —
            not a permanent junk drawer.

        VO: Try this: answer the same coding question twice — once with a whole-file paste, once with a neighbourhood slice — and compare the model's focus.
    }
    @slides (
        {
            id title
            transition fade
            background brand-dark
            kicker Advanced · 04
            heading Context and tokens
            body Compose a slice. Do not paste the whole project by habit.
            asset logo
            notes Context is a composed model — not a single blob labelled the project.
        }
        {
            id contrast
            transition none
            background brand-panel
            heading Bad paste vs good slice
            body Same question. Different focus for the model.
            code_lang txt
            code Bad: paste every .rq file / Good: neighbourhood for login_api + one question
            notes Token discipline is a product feature and a habit.
        }
        {
            id pins
            transition fade
            background brand-panel
            heading Pins are exceptions
            body Manual context is for the thing you are reasoning about now — not a junk drawer.
            asset chat-search
            notes Summaries and counts first; expand a dimension when you mean to.
        }
        {
            id try-this
            transition fade
            background brand-dark
            heading Try this
