}

adv_05_comment_references {
    Outcome: place rq:[…] comment links in implementation; navigate from code comments to ideas; understand round-trip traceability with file references.
    Runtime: 8–9 min.
    Related: [references_in_functional_code_comments] [any_file_scope]
    @example {
        ```ts
        // src/login.ts
        export async function login(email: string, password: string) {
          // rq:[password_rules]
          if (!password) throw new Error("empty password");
          // rq:["../reqs/auth.rq".login_api] }
        ```
    }
    @script {
        SCR: Open `login.ts`. Add a comment reference to password_rules above the empty-password guard. Show link underline / navigation.

        VO: File references point requirements at code. Comment references point code back at requirements —
            same graph, entered from the implementation side.

        SCR: Add a qualified comment link to `login_api`. Flip to activity bar while focused in the TypeScript file.

        VO: The prefix `rq:` marks the token for tooling. It works across languages because it lives in comments.

        SCR: Optional 20s: same pattern in a Python snippet to stress [general_purpose] / any-language comments.

        VO: Try this: add one comment reference in a test file pointing at `password_rules`.
    }
    @slides (
        {
            id title
            transition fade
            background brand-dark
            kicker Advanced · 05
            heading Comment references
            body Point code back at requirements — same graph, other door.
            asset logo
            notes File references point requirements at code. Comment references reverse the arrow.
        }
        {
            id rq-token
            transition none
            background brand-panel
            heading The rq: token
            body Lives in comments, so it works across languages.
            code_lang ts
            code // rq:[password_rules]
            notes The prefix rq: marks the token for tooling.
        }
        {
            id round-trip
            transition fade
            background brand-panel
            heading Round-trip traceability
            body Requirements → files. Files → requirements. Both stay in the graph.
            code_lang ts
            code // rq:["../reqs/auth.rq".login_api]
            asset file-link
            notes Same graph, entered from the implementation side.
        }
        {
            id try-this
            transition fade
            background brand-dark
            heading Try this
            body Add one comment reference in a test file pointing at password_rules.
            fragments Next — HTML export
            notes Optional: show the same pattern in Python for any-language comments.
        }
    )
}

