adv_08_modelling_patterns {
    Outcome: leave viewers with durable modelling habits — thin ideas, explicit links, purposeful attributes, maps over dumps — including one non-software example.
    Runtime: 10–11 min.
    Related: [simplicity] [general_purpose] [cartographic_map] [mission_statement]
    @example {
        ```rq
        // Vignette B — editorial / ops, still .rq
        // reqs/newsletter.rq
        issue_brief {
            June issue theme: "small tools with sharp edges".
            Lead piece must cite [interview_lee].
            @status draft
            @tags (
                editorial
            )
        }

        interview_lee {
            Interview with Lee about maintaining a tiny CLI used in production.
            Assets live under ["./media/interviews/"]
        }

        production_checklist {
            Before send: spellcheck, link check, unsubscribe footer, [issue_brief] theme echoed in subject line.
        }
        ```
    }
    @script {
        SCR: Title: "Patterns that age well". Quick recap montage of the advanced series (5s).

        VO: Advanced reqlan is not more syntax — it's better judgement about what deserves a name,
            what deserves a link, and what deserves to stay out of the prompt.

        SCR: Open the newsletter vignette file. Navigate links. Show this is still the same language.

        VO: The language is general-purpose. Software is the common case, not the only case.
            If you can name a concept and care about its neighbours, it can live in a `.rq` graph.

        SCR: Return to the product demo. On a whiteboard slide (or typed list), four patterns:
            1. One idea, one job
            2. Links over duplication
            3. Attributes that drive a view
            4. Maps you choose, never mandatory full dumps

        VO: Those four keep you aligned with why the project exists —
            a structured semantic framework for people working with LLMs, with ergonomic definition and consumption.

        SCR: End card: link pack from [phonebook] — site, docs, marketplace, GitHub. "Write the idea. Link the neighbour. Ship the slice."

        VO: Thanks for watching. Write the idea. Link the neighbour. Ship the slice.
    }
    @slides (
        {
            id title
            transition fade
            background brand-dark
            kicker Advanced · 08
            heading Patterns that age well
            body Not more syntax — better judgement about names, links, and prompt size.
            asset logo
            notes Advanced reqlan is not more syntax.
        }
        {
            id vignette
            transition none
            background brand-panel
            heading Same language, other domain
            body Editorial briefs and ops checklists are still named ideas with neighbours.
            code_lang rq
            code issue_brief { June theme… cite [interview_lee]. status draft }
            notes Software is the common case, not the only case.
        }
        {
            id four
            transition fade
            background brand-panel
            heading Four durable habits
            body Keep the graph readable for people and models alike.
            code_lang txt
            code 1. One idea, one job / 2. Links over duplication / 3. Attributes that drive a view / 4. Maps you choose
            notes A structured semantic framework for people working with LLMs.
        }
        {
